Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||11-15-2001||01:33 PM||||I can't believe I actually read their entire thread.  Couldn't tell when their statements ended and their signatures began (now I really understand why Cliff wants us limiting our sigs).  Even most of those who "approved" of your car- were kind of dinks about it.  <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Anyway, good kill - even if you are insecure about it being "just a Fiero" and feel the need to beg for approval by listing how little it's cost you. I'm feeling generous today so you can have some approval. Don't get all cocky about it or the next time you beg I will not be as lenient on someone like yourself who owns a little cheap car.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Good Kill, and you do have a very nice ride! <BR>The C5 you raced was most likely bone stock, or even an auto with the 2.73 rearend. My 6 speed with intake/exhaust alone pulled 12.80s @ 112 on stock tires. So sorry budy, if this Vette had any basic mods, you would have been toast! <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I could build something faster with less than 6k, but it wouldn't look as good, not by a long shot.  Good job on building a nice looking fiero. I used to like the GTs. A buddy of mine had one back in high school and it would really move for what it was. GM could have done a lot with the fiero.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think I'll ever buy a 'vette- Not that they're not nice & fast, just to common for me.  IMO anyway...||||reg||1
